# VITE_API_URL: Base URL of the FastAPI backend (no /api suffix).
#
# Unset:
#   - `npm run dev` calls http://localhost:8000.
#   - A production build calls the origin it is served from. That is right when
#     the backend serves dist/ (FRONTEND_DIST), but on a static host (Vercel,
#     Netlify, ...) it points at the static site itself, so detection requests
#     fail with "Cannot reach the backend" / "Unexpected response" until a
#     backend URL is set: either build with VITE_API_URL, or have the visitor
#     enter one in the Demo's API Config panel.
#
# Set it when the backend lives somewhere else. It is baked in at build time, so
# change it and rebuild. The backend must be reachable over HTTPS from an HTTPS
# page, and its CORS_ORIGINS must include the site's origin.
# VITE_API_URL="https://your-backend.example.com"

# ======================================================================================
# Hub-and-spoke: one repo, three surfaces
# ======================================================================================
# Every VITE_* value is baked in at BUILD time. Change one, rebuild.
#
#   hub      Portfolio: engineering notes, live benchmark, case studies, intake.
#            Also serves /demo and /fitness, so it is the default and what
#            localhost / preview URLs get.
#   lab      The CV Auto-Labeler on its own (e.g. lab.example.com). `/` opens it.
#   fitness  The fitness app on its own (e.g. fit.example.com). `/` opens it.
#
# Mode comes from VITE_APP_MODE if set, otherwise from the hostname: lab.* means
# lab, fitness.* means fitness, anything else is the hub. Add exact hostnames to
# the two lists below for domains that do not follow the naming convention.
# For separate Cloudflare Pages projects, VITE_APP_MODE is the clearest choice.
# VITE_APP_MODE=hub                 # hub | lab | fitness
# VITE_LAB_HOSTS=labeler.example.com,other.example.com
# VITE_FITNESS_HOSTS=fit.example.com

# Where each surface lives, for cross-links. Leave a URL unset and links stay
# in-app routes (what you want in one deployment and in local dev). In a
# standalone spoke, VITE_HUB_URL is what the "Portfolio" button and the
# "Engineered by Farai" credit point at; without it they are plain text / hidden.
# VITE_HUB_URL=https://example.com
# VITE_LAB_URL=https://lab.example.com
# VITE_FITNESS_URL=https://fit.example.com

# Intake on the hub. The form composes an email in the visitor's mail app (no
# server). Defaults to the address already published on the Contact page.
# VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=you@example.com
# VITE_BOOKING_URL=https://cal.com/you/20min      # optional: a "pick a time" link

# ======================================================================================
# Large files: models and runtimes (Cloudflare Pages 25 MiB-per-file limit)
# ======================================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages rejects any single file over 25 MiB. The ONNX Runtime WebGPU
# wasm is ~28 MiB, and bigger YOLO exports (yolo11m, anything at 960) are tens of
# MB. So for Pages, serve them from object storage (Cloudflare R2, a CDN):
#
#   VITE_MODEL_BASE_URL            .onnx models and MediaPipe .task files.
#                                  Default /models (the repo's public/models).
#                                  Layout under it:  yolo11n.onnx, yolo11s.onnx, ...,
#                                  penguin.onnx, pose/pose_landmarker_full.task, ...
#   VITE_ORT_WASM_BASE_URL         ONNX Runtime wasm. Default: bundled at /ort/.
#                                  When set, the wasm is left OUT of the build.
#                                  Upload:  ort-wasm-simd-threaded.jsep.mjs and
#                                  ort-wasm-simd-threaded.jsep.wasm
#                                  (from node_modules/onnxruntime-web/dist).
#   VITE_MEDIAPIPE_WASM_BASE_URL   MediaPipe wasm. Default: bundled at /mediapipe/wasm
#                                  (4 files, each under 25 MiB, fine to keep).
#
# The bucket must send CORS headers (Access-Control-Allow-Origin: the site origin
# or *) because the browser fetches these cross-origin. The build checks the
# limit: locally it warns; on Cloudflare Pages (CF_PAGES=1) or with
# ENFORCE_ASSET_LIMIT=1 it FAILS the build and names the oversized file.
# VITE_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://models.example.com
# VITE_ORT_WASM_BASE_URL=https://models.example.com/ort
# VITE_MEDIAPIPE_WASM_BASE_URL=https://models.example.com/mediapipe/wasm

# ======================================================================================
# Pro and pilot unlocks (no server: checkout links + offline license keys)
# ======================================================================================
# Checkout links open in a new tab. They must be https. A "{plan}" in the value is
# replaced with the plan id (cv-pro, solo_12week, solo_year, pilot) for providers
# that accept a reference in the link. Paystack, Dodo, Stripe payment links all work.
# VITE_CV_CHECKOUT_URL=https://paystack.com/pay/cv-pro
# VITE_FITNESS_CHECKOUT_ZAR_URL=https://paystack.com/pay/fitness-{plan}
# VITE_FITNESS_CHECKOUT_USD_URL=https://checkout.dodopayments.com/buy/fitness-{plan}
#
# License keys are checked in the browser against this PUBLIC key (a JWK, JSON on
# one line). Create the pair and issue keys with:  node scripts/license.mjs
# Keep the private key out of this repo. Browser checks can be bypassed by a
# determined person, so treat this as an honest unlock for client-side features,
# not DRM, and enforce anything that costs you money on a server.
# VITE_LICENSE_PUBLIC_KEY='{"kty":"EC","crv":"P-256","x":"...","y":"..."}'
#
# A testing switch that unlocks Pro with one click. It is ON in `npm run dev`
# and OFF in production builds unless you set this. Never enable it on a live site.
# VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_UNLOCK=true

# ======================================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages: deployment notes
# ======================================================================================
# Build command:           npm run build
# Build output directory:  dist
# Environment:             NODE_VERSION=22   (any current LTS), plus the VITE_* above.
#                          Set them for BOTH Production and Preview if you use previews.
# SPA routing:             public/_redirects (/* /index.html 200) is already in place.
# Headers/caching:         public/_headers is already in place (immutable /assets/*,
#                          camera=(self) permissions policy, nosniff).
#
# One repo, three sites: create three Pages projects from this repo, each with its
# own VITE_APP_MODE (hub / lab / fitness) and custom domain, e.g.
#   example.com      VITE_APP_MODE=hub      VITE_LAB_URL=https://lab.example.com  VITE_FITNESS_URL=https://fit.example.com
#   lab.example.com  VITE_APP_MODE=lab      VITE_HUB_URL=https://example.com
#   fit.example.com  VITE_APP_MODE=fitness  VITE_HUB_URL=https://example.com
# Or ship one project and let hostnames pick the mode (lab.* / fitness.*).
#
# Sizes: with VITE_ORT_WASM_BASE_URL set, the build contains no file near the limit.
# Put the model and runtime files in R2, attach a public domain or custom domain to
# the bucket, and add a CORS rule for your site origins.
